raw_text:
So looks like this is not fundamentally a new bug. This, for example, doesn't work in M81:

<style>
  @keyframes test {
    from { font-size: 1em; }
    to { font-size: 1em; }
  }

  textarea {
    font-size: 1em;
  }

  textarea:first-child {
    animation: test 1s linear paused
  }
</style>
<p>
  Textareas below should be the same size
</p>
<textarea>Hello World</textarea>
<textarea>Hello World</textarea>

However, it's much easier to reach the broken state in M83+.

So far it looks like it's caused by FontBuilder's adjustments to the specified font-size that take place when the generic font family changes to/from monospace. It's probably intending to check the parent style's font description, but instead checks its own description, which it assumes is the same as the parent's (which it's not).

